capability encode/replace-with-a-sign  a character an encoding has no bytes for written as `?` or another sign
  heroes  refused: the standard's error modes are failing and the HTML reference alone; a `?` loses the character in silence, which `encode` failing says aloud and `encode_html` keeps readable
  go      encoding.ReplaceUnsupported, encoding.ASCIISub
