  dotnet  EncoderReplacementFallback, EncoderReplacementFallback.DefaultString, EncoderFallback.ReplacementFallback, Encoding.EncoderFallback

## Error modes the standard does not have

capability errors/ignore  what cannot be read or written dropped in silence
  heroes  refused: a byte or a character lost with no sign is the silent loss the standard's modes exist to prevent
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  codecs.ignore_errors
  java    CodingErrorAction.IGNORE
  dotnet  -

capability errors/escapes  what cannot be read or written kept as an escape: `\x80`, `\N{...}`, a lone surrogate
  heroes  refused: a `str` holds UTF-8 alone, so a lone surrogate cannot be kept; `bytes.format_escaped` writes bytes as escapes for a person to read
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  codecs.backslashreplace_errors, codecs.namereplace_errors, surrogateescape, surrogatepass
  java    -
  dotnet  -

capability errors/handlers  a function of the program's called on each error, or a registry of them
  heroes  refused: a handler registered by name is a mutable global, which the language has not; a program that wants another rule decodes with `decode_strict` and reads `valid_prefix_len`
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  codecs.register_error, codecs.lookup_error
  java    CharsetDecoder.implOnMalformedInput, CharsetDecoder.implOnUnmappableCharacter, CharsetDecoder.implReplaceWith, CharsetEncoder.implOnMalformedInput, CharsetEncoder.implOnUnmappableCharacter, CharsetEncoder.implReplaceWith
  dotnet  EncoderFallback, DecoderFallback, EncoderFallbackBuffer, DecoderFallbackBuffer, EncoderFallback.CreateFallbackBuffer, DecoderFallback.CreateFallbackBuffer, EncoderFallback.MaxCharCount, DecoderFallback.MaxCharCount

## Encodings outside the standard

capability isomorphic/latin1  bytes read as the characters U+0000 to U+00FF of their numbers, and written back, the Infra standard's isomorphic decoding
  heroes  unicode/encodings.decode_isomorphic, unicode/encodings.encode_isomorphic
  go      charmap.ISO8859_1
  rust    encoding_rs::mem::decode_latin1, mem::encode_latin1_lossy, mem::convert_latin1_to_utf8, mem::convert_latin1_to_str, mem::convert_utf8_to_latin1_lossy, mem::is_str_latin1, mem::is_utf8_latin1, mem::utf8_latin1_up_to, mem::str_latin1_up_to
  python  codecs.latin_1_decode, codecs.latin_1_encode, the codec latin_1
  java    StandardCharsets.ISO_8859_1
  dotnet  Encoding.Latin1
  note    the standard reads the label `latin1` and `iso-8859-1` as windows-1252, as every browser does; a protocol that means each byte as its own number, an HTTP header among them, asks this instead

capability ascii/strict  bytes read as ASCII, failing on a byte above 127
  heroes  bytes.is_ascii
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  codecs.ascii_decode, codecs.ascii_encode, the codec ascii
  java    StandardCharsets.US_ASCII
  dotnet  Encoding.ASCII
  note    bytes that pass are text as they are, `bytes.to_text`; the standard reads `ascii` and `us-ascii` as windows-1252

capability utf16/units  UTF-16 bytes with no byte order mark read and written, in either order
  heroes  unicode/encodings.decode, unicode/encodings.encode
  go      unicode.UTF16, unicode.BigEndian, unicode.LittleEndian, unicode.Endianness
  rust    String::from_utf16le, String::from_utf16be, String::from_utf16le_lossy, String::from_utf16be_lossy
  python  codecs.utf_16_be_decode, codecs.utf_16_be_encode, codecs.utf_16_le_decode, codecs.utf_16_le_encode, codecs.utf_16_decode, codecs.utf_16_encode, codecs.utf_16_ex_decode, the codecs utf_16, utf_16_be, utf_16_le
  java    StandardCharsets.UTF_16, StandardCharsets.UTF_16BE, StandardCharsets.UTF_16LE, x-UTF-16LE-BOM
  dotnet  Encoding.Unicode, Encoding.BigEndianUnicode
  note    the standard defines UTF-16BE and UTF-16LE decoders and no encoder, and a browser writes UTF-8 in their place (`output_encoding`); written here, since every other library writes them

capability utf32/units  UTF-32 bytes read and written
  heroes  refused: no browser reads UTF-32 and the standard names no such encoding; its four bytes a character are `bytes.encode_u32_le` and `bytes.decode_u32_le` over the code points, and `unicode.from_code_points` checks them
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  codecs.utf_32_decode, codecs.utf_32_encode, codecs.utf_32_be_decode, codecs.utf_32_be_encode, codecs.utf_32_le_decode, codecs.utf_32_le_encode, codecs.utf_32_ex_decode, codecs.BOM_UTF32, codecs.BOM_UTF32_BE, codecs.BOM_UTF32_LE, codecs.BOM32_BE, codecs.BOM32_LE, codecs.BOM64_BE, codecs.BOM64_LE, the codecs utf_32, utf_32_be, utf_32_le
